Spec: Feature Issue 91 - Cleanup Orphaned Program Runs on Scheduler Startup

Platform: Rust/Linux

Purpose:
  Update orphaned `program_runs` entries whose `exit_code` or `success` is `NULL` to `exit_code = 2`, `success = false`, and `finished_at = COALESCE(finished_at, CURRENT_TIMESTAMP)` when `mitm_scheduler-server` starts up. Issue: https://github.com/Zheng-Bote/mitm_core-layer/issues/91

References:
  ../../core-layer.sdd
  ../architecture.sdd

Owns:
  ./**

Can modify:
  /mitm_scheduler-server/src/db.rs
  /mitm_scheduler-server/src/main.rs
  /mitm_scheduler-server/Cargo.toml
  /mitm_scheduler-server/CHANGELOG.md

Must:
  On startup of `mitm_scheduler-server` (after binding the singleton UDS listener and before starting `@CronScheduler`), `@Repository.cleanup_unfinished_program_runs` updates every row in `program_runs` where `exit_code IS NULL OR success IS NULL` to `exit_code = 2`, `success = false`, and `finished_at = COALESCE(finished_at, CURRENT_TIMESTAMP)`.
  When one or more rows are updated, `mitm_scheduler-server` logs the count to STDOUT and `system_logs` (`WARN`, component `scheduler-server`).

Must not:
  Modify `program_runs` rows before the singleton UDS check confirms no other scheduler instance is running.

Tasks:
  [x] #1 Add `@Repository.cleanup_unfinished_program_runs` in `mitm_scheduler-server/src/db.rs`.
  [x] #2 Call `@Repository.cleanup_unfinished_program_runs` during startup in `mitm_scheduler-server/src/main.rs` after binding the UDS socket.
  [x] #3 Bump `mitm-scheduler-server` version to `1.3.6` and update `CHANGELOG.md`.

Done when:
  `cargo test` and `cargo build --release` succeed across the `core-layer` workspace.

Scenario: orphaned program_runs row at startup
  Given `program_runs` contains a row with `exit_code` `NULL` or `success` `NULL`
  When `mitm_scheduler-server` starts and acquires the UDS listener
  Then that row has `exit_code = 2`, `success = false`, and a non-null `finished_at`
